sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Client
  participant E as ESTS
  participant A as Authenticator app<br/>(user device)
  Note over C,E: Common prefix: authorize and GetCredentialType (Figure 2)<br/>Credentials.RemoteNgcParams{SessionIdentifier, Entropy, Application}
  C->>E: POST /common/GetOneTimeCode (JSON)
  Note over C,E: headers: canary, client-request-id<br/>body: Channel=Authenticator, FlowToken=sFT, OriginalRequest=sCtx,<br/>OldDeviceCode=RemoteNgcParams.SessionIdentifier
  E-->>C: 200 JSON: RemoteNgcParams{SessionIdentifier, Entropy,<br/>DefaultType: 3, UserCode}
  E-)A: push notification (out of band)
  Note over C,E: Use returned SessionIdentifier and Entropy, display number match
  loop repeat
    Note over C,E: pending within a finite local deadline, stop on cancellation or<br/>failure
    C->>E: POST {urlSessionState}?code={SessionIdentifier}
    Note over C,E: header canary, body {DeviceCode}
    E-->>C: 200 {AuthorizationState: 0}  (pending)
  end
  A->>E: user approves number match
  C->>E: POST {urlSessionState}?code={SessionIdentifier}
  E-->>C: 200 {AuthorizationState: 2}  (approved)
  C->>E: POST /{tenant}/login (form)
  Note over C,E: code, psRNGCSLK, login, loginfmt, psRNGCEntropy,<br/>flowToken, canary, ctx
  alt authorization code issued
    E-->>C: 302 Location: {redirect_uri}?code=...&session_state=...
    Note over E,C: + ESTSAUTH, ESTSAUTHPERSISTENT, CCState, ...
    Note over C,E: ESTS complete: upstream OAuth handoff (section 2.12)
  else interrupt
    E-->>C: 200 HTML with $Config (KMSI, ProofUp, ...) (Figure 13)
  end
